   {
    "id": "i2",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     34,
     44
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link AlphabetConverter}. <p> An {@link AlphabetConverter} maps every character of an <em>original</em> alphabet to a fixed-length sequence of characters drawn from an <em>encoding</em> alphabet. Characters listed in the <em>do-not-encode</em> set are passed through unchanged. The tests below exercise round-trip encoding/decoding for several alphabet pairs as well as the construction-time and decoding-time error conditions. </p>"
   },
   {
    "id": "i3",
    "kind": "LineComment",
    "lines": [
     47,
     47
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "--- Alphabets used as building blocks for the converters under test. ---"
   },
   {
    "id": "i4",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     49,
     49
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "The space character plus the 26 lower-case English letters."
   },
   {
    "id": "i5",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     53,
     53
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Digits, both letter cases of the English alphabet, and a space."
   },
   {
    "id": "i6",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     58,
     58
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Digits, the lower-case English alphabet, and a space."
   },
   {
    "id": "i7",
